1
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,929
[majestic music playing]

2
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:16,349
OCTOBER 15, 1890
3RD STAGE

3
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,311
[announcer] <i>All of our racers
have finally reached the Rocky Mountains,</i>

4
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:24,315
<i>en route to their next finish line
in scenic Cañon City.</i>

5
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:28,319
<i>These majestic peaks are, without a doubt,
the greatest challenge</i>

6
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:31,781
<i>our indomitable jockeys will face
in this third stage.</i>

7
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:36,036
How each of them will tame these wilds
is truly anyone's guess.

8
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:39,372
[groaning in frustration]

9
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,375
{\an8}Damn it all. This is horrible!

10
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:46,004
{\an8}[thinking] <i>Even if I place first
in this third stage, and I aim to,</i>

11
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:49,507
{\an8}<i>my total points will still only be 136.</i>

12
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:53,261
<i>That bastard Dio is sitting pretty at 150.</i>

13
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:55,472
<i>It won't be enough to overtake him.</i>

14
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:57,432
<i>Not to mention...</i> [grunts]

15
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:00,018
<i>...Johnny's hot on his heels.</i>

16
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:02,812
<i>If he gets first,
he'll have 180 points to his name</i>

17
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:04,773
<i>and leave us all in the dust.</i>

18
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:07,984
<i>I'm first. He's second. He agreed to that.</i>

19
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:11,529
<i>I guess a promise from Johnny Joestar
ain't worth the spit in his mouth</i>

20
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:12,781
<i>when he makes it.</i>

21
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:13,698
[Johnny] Hmm.

22
00:01:14,282 --> 00:01:16,576
[Gyro] <i>Dio and Sand Man are both
beating me on points,</i>

23
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:21,164
<i>and there's no way they won't earn more
in this leg of the race. Son of a bitch!</i>

24
00:01:21,873 --> 00:01:24,417
Please, Lord, just give them
a goose egg apiece.

25
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:26,127
[Johnny] Gyro, look.

26
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,212
[Gyro] Huh?

27
00:01:28,254 --> 00:01:31,091
- Isn't that Dio on the ground over there?
- [Gyro] Hmm?

28
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:35,178
Something feels off, though.

29
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,222
Let's see.

30
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:44,854
Little Lord Fauntleroy
must've taken a tumble.

31
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:47,607
There's blood on his face.
On his helmet too.

32
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:51,069
[thinking] <i>Give my regards to Lady Luck.
Nyo-ho.</i>

33
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:53,780
You think he fell? Him, of all people?

34
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:55,865
Doesn't seem likely.

35
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,909
[Gyro] And down for the count.

36
00:01:59,744 --> 00:02:02,872
[Johnny] From the looks of it,
he's going to fall behind for sure.

37
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:05,333
He might be out of the running for good.

38
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:06,501
Let's keep going.

39
00:02:06,584 --> 00:02:10,004
Really? I didn't take you
for the cold-blooded type, Johnny.

40
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:13,800
While I'm glad young master Dio
got tossed ass over kettle,

41
00:02:13,883 --> 00:02:16,970
we should at least make sure
he isn't knocking on death's door.

42
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:18,888
Let's give him a look.

43
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:22,308
Diego Brando has done nothing
to merit our concern, Gyro.

44
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:24,227
[Gyro] Well, look at that.

45
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:27,147
Pretty small-minded of you there,
golden boy.

46
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:29,149
Dio can't be trusted.

47
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:33,862
True, he's the crown prince
of England's horse-racing scene,

48
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:38,408
but there's no end to his villainy
when riches or victory are on the line.

49
00:02:38,908 --> 00:02:41,119
I've heard so many stories.

50
00:02:41,744 --> 00:02:43,872
<i>When he was just 20 years old,</i>

51
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:46,166
<i>he married a woman who was 83.</i>

52
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:49,586
<i>Turns out, Dio's new bride
was sitting on a fortune.</i>

53
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:57,218
<i>Not six months later, she was dead.</i>

54
00:02:57,302 --> 00:03:00,346
<i>Rumor had it,
Dio was impatient to cash in.</i>

55
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:05,518
Quit your meandering
and just say it already.

56
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:09,147
Dio might be faking an injury down there
to lure us in.

57
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:12,942
For all we know,
he's in cahoots with our assailants.

58
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:14,611
[Gyro sighs]

59
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:16,696
[somber music playing]

60
00:03:17,197 --> 00:03:19,782
Pulling the wool over your eyes
would make a lot of sense

61
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:23,119
if he were losing to you,
but he's in first place.

62
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:25,121
- So what does he gain by it?
- [horse whickers]

63
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:26,581
I'm gonna check on him.

64
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:44,182
Hey, Dio. Rise and shine.

65
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:46,559
You want us to get you a rescue team?

66
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:47,936
Just say the word.

67
00:03:48,561 --> 00:03:50,897
[Dio groaning softly]

68
00:03:53,691 --> 00:03:55,693
[mysterious music playing]

69
00:03:56,402 --> 00:03:57,862
[growls softly]

70
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:00,198
[Johnny gasps]

71
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:05,536
[thinking] <i>His fingers, they're hideous.</i>

72
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:10,208
<i>Are those scabs? What could've left them?</i>

73
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:11,960
[Dio grunts]

74
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:15,672
What do you care, plebeian?
Get out of my sight already. Both of you.

75
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:20,260
Go on. Either way,
I, Dio, will leave you in the dust.

76
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:24,347
<i>Nyo-ho-ho.</i> Alive enough to be an ass, huh?

77
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:25,974
Good enough for me.

78
00:04:26,724 --> 00:04:27,850
[Johnny] Huh?

79
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:29,644
[panting]

80
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:31,354
[horse neighs]

81
00:04:32,146 --> 00:04:33,564
[Gyro] Onward, Johnny.

82
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:36,276
[Johnny gasps] Y... yeah.

83
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:37,360
[horse whickers]

84
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,862
[panting]

85
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:42,824
[suspenseful music playing]

86
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:45,243
[Dio grunts]

87
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:47,787
[mysterious growling]

88
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:58,589
[jaunty music playing]

89
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:11,686
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

90
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,985
[lyrics in Japanese]

91
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:31,391
{\an8}3RD STAGE -DAY 5- THE ROCKY MOUNTAINS
ABOUT 240 MILES FROM MONUMENT VALLEY

92
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:34,560
{\an8}Gyro, at the rate we're going,

93
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,979
{\an8}we'll need two more days
to cross over the Rockies.

94
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:40,441
That mountain.
It's the one I've been looking for.

95
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:43,945
It's about nine miles off.
Can we get there today?

96
00:06:44,028 --> 00:06:45,154
Nah, why risk it?

97
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:48,533
The sun's about to set.
Our horses need rest.

98
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:54,205
[Johnny thinking] <i>No doubt about it.
The next piece of the corpse is up there.</i>

99
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:56,999
<i>We just have to track it down.</i>

100
00:06:57,083 --> 00:06:58,626
- [Gyro] Hey, Johnny.
- [Johnny gasps]

101
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:00,628
- [horse neighs]
- Valkyrie's spooked by something.

102
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:01,921
Huh.

103
00:07:02,004 --> 00:07:03,131
[tense music playing]

104
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:04,632
[gasps]

105
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:07,510
{\an8}We've got company.

106
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:08,970
It's Dio!

107
00:07:12,014 --> 00:07:13,433
{\an8}Whatever was wrong before,

108
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:16,102
{\an8}I'm sensing a lot of power
coming off of him now.

109
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:17,145
{\an8}Keep your guard up!

110
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:20,398
- We can't let him pass us, no matter what!
- [Johnny] Mm.

111
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:23,693
[Dio] Oh, ye of little faith,
you wound me, sirs.

112
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:26,237
The day is all but over. Look at the sun.

113
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:30,658
{\an8}There is a humble village ahead of us.
We should stay the night.

114
00:07:30,741 --> 00:07:32,577
{\an8}Roughing it here can be deadly.

115
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,996
{\an8}Many creatures
would attack you in the dark.

116
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:40,334
The other day,
several such beasts accosted me at dusk.

117
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:43,421
A great number of cougars and rattlesnakes
approached me.

118
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,756
They made to block my path,

119
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,551
leaving my beleaguered horse
no way forward.

120
00:07:48,634 --> 00:07:49,510
[Gyro] Huh?

121
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,721
As I was about to double back,

122
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:55,933
one of the species was kind enough
to move aside and allow my egress.

123
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:58,728
They were only beasts,
but so well-mannered.

124
00:07:59,228 --> 00:08:02,523
Which of the animals do you think
extended me that courtesy?

125
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:04,692
Was it the cougars? Or the rattlesnakes?

126
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:07,320
The answer is

127
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,489
the rattlesnakes, of course.

128
00:08:09,572 --> 00:08:11,741
They let me through. That's the truth.

129
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:14,410
I suppose one could say
they moved slither and yon for me.

130
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,328
- Huh?
- Huh?

131
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,498
A clever bit of word-play,
you philistines.

132
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:20,124
Do try to keep up, would you?

133
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:23,711
But then the cougars decided
they wanted to eat my faithful steed.

134
00:08:23,794 --> 00:08:26,422
Silver Bullet told them "neigh."
So they asked again.

135
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:29,258
But "neigh, neigh, neigh"
was the only reply.

136
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:30,468
[Johnny groans softly]

137
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:32,970
How wonderful!

138
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:36,766
This little tête-à-tête
is a balm for the soul, is it not?

139
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:39,352
I fell from my horse, but now I'm fine.

140
00:08:39,435 --> 00:08:42,939
It gave me a second wind.
A shame this day is almost done.

141
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:46,150
Listen up, Diego.
You'd better keep your distance.

142
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,610
We're not travelling with you.

143
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:50,446
How very fierce of you, Johnny Joestar.

144
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:55,034
{\an8}You performed splendidly
in the first and second stages alike.

145
00:08:55,117 --> 00:08:58,871
{\an8}I heard your racing days were done.
Your comeback is so heroic.

146
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:00,790
- [Johnny grunts]
- [boom]

147
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:05,753
- [creature chitters]
- [Johnny gasps]

148
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:09,090
[gasps]

149
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:14,011
Ta-da! Can the two of you ride like this,
adroit horsemen that you are?

150
00:09:14,095 --> 00:09:15,471
- [Gyro] Uh...
- [Dio] Hup!

151
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:17,890
Hup!

152
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:19,141
Hup.

153
00:09:19,225 --> 00:09:21,811
[Gyro] Hey, Johnny.
What's up with this guy?

154
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:23,563
[Dio] Behold!

155
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:26,732
[Gyro] Mr. Genius Jockey's
ready for a straightjacket.

156
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:30,403
Something isn't right.
That much is certain.

157
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:32,738
Gyro, tell me we're not bunking with him.

158
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:34,740
The thought of it's making me ill.

159
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:35,658
[Dio] Hup!

160
00:09:35,741 --> 00:09:38,536
[Gyro] But there is
a lot of dangerous wildlife up here.

161
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:40,705
The village is the safest bet.

162
00:09:40,788 --> 00:09:44,750
Correct! The only bet worth placing
if you value your lives.

163
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:45,918
[Johnny grunts]

164
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:47,837
How the hell did he hear us?

165
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,218
[man] Welcome!

166
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:56,596
[villagers cheering]

167
00:09:57,179 --> 00:09:59,807
- [man 2] Welcome to our humble abode.
- [man 3] We've been waiting!

168
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:02,310
[Gyro] A tiny little village
in the Rocky Mountains,

169
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:05,021
and they still know
about the Steel Ball Run.

170
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:09,400
Where did Dio get off to?
I lost sight of him.

171
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:13,738
Who cares? Maybe he's showing
some of the locals his acrobatics routine.

172
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,157
[Johnny] I'm not kidding, Gyro.

173
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:19,201
I refuse to sleep
in the same place as that man.

174
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:23,372
Dio might be a top-notch racer,
but he's a horrible human being.

175
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,625
I wouldn't put it past him at all
to poison our food

176
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:28,377
or tamper with our horses. Would you?

177
00:10:29,211 --> 00:10:30,338
[Gyro] Nah, you're right.

178
00:10:30,921 --> 00:10:34,800
Let's keep our eyes peeled,
same as we do when we sleep outdoors.

179
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:37,219
Hey, we got a stove.

180
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:40,056
Lucky, that. I'll grab us some firewood.

181
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:42,558
[gentle music playing]

182
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:57,573
[faint clatter]

183
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:58,658
Hmm?

184
00:10:59,241 --> 00:11:01,285
[suspenseful music playing]

185
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:04,830
[Johnny gasps]

186
00:11:05,831 --> 00:11:06,791
Dio.

187
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:12,672
[gasps]

188
00:11:17,343 --> 00:11:18,594
[Dio gulping]

189
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:19,679
[Johnny gasps]

190
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:26,435
Hmm.

191
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:28,646
[Dio sniffs]

192
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,816
The welcome scent of coffee.

193
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:36,779
Who's brewing coffee in there?
The aroma's to die for.

194
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,990
Wh... what are you doing
skulking around, Dio?

195
00:11:40,574 --> 00:11:41,659
Not a thing.

196
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:42,952
[Johnny] I doubt that.

197
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:46,372
Hey! Who said you could come in here?

198
00:11:46,455 --> 00:11:49,083
Ah, I imagine you were unnerved

199
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:51,585
by the sight of my eating rocks
a moment ago.

200
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:53,045
[Johnny grunts softly]

201
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:57,258
[Dio] You really don't know?
They're digestive aids, Joestar.

202
00:11:57,341 --> 00:11:59,802
They help to break down the food
in one's stomach.

203
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:01,679
They're called "gastroliths."

204
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:04,640
Most carnivorous creatures
rely on such things.

205
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:06,100
They grant good health.

206
00:12:06,183 --> 00:12:09,019
Birds and crocodiles
both use them to great effect.

207
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:11,981
But I digress. Your coffee.

208
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:15,192
Not of the peerless beans
of Jamaica's Blue Mountain,

209
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,194
but it calls to me nonetheless.

210
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:19,822
Would you indulge me a cup of it?

211
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:24,160
That was a pretty bad fall you took.
I saw blood on your face and your helmet.

212
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:28,330
Don't blow it out of proportion.
I haven't a scratch on me.

213
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:30,082
Why are your gloves still on?

214
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:33,127
Nights are cold in the Rockies.
It's October now.

215
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,129
They'll come off when I wash.

216
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:37,840
You can spare a little coffee. Be a pal.

217
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:41,886
We're not friends, Diego Brando.
I don't trust you.

218
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:44,346
Yes, you can have some.

219
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:46,807
But I want you out of here
the moment you're done.

220
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:48,893
[suspenseful music continues]

221
00:12:51,937 --> 00:12:52,813
[Dio grunts]

222
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:54,398
[sniffs]

223
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:56,984
In that case, which one should I drink?

224
00:12:57,067 --> 00:13:00,070
I'd rather we not share a cup tonight.

225
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:03,073
What do you mean?
There's only coffee in one.

226
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:06,285
Don't you see it?
The others are cans of food.

227
00:13:06,368 --> 00:13:07,745
They don't look anything alike.

228
00:13:08,537 --> 00:13:09,830
Think I can't see?

229
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:11,707
- [Johnny gasps]
- Don't mock me.

230
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:15,586
You would be shocked how well I can see.

231
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:17,838
Even better at night, truth be told.

232
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:20,257
Much about me would shock you, I wager.

233
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:22,510
Now which one is it?

234
00:13:22,593 --> 00:13:23,844
[sniffs]

235
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:25,179
Which one?

236
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:29,683
Stop it! Like I said,
there's only coffee in one cup.

237
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:30,976
- [Dio grunts]
- [Johnny gasps]

238
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:35,940
What an odd guy.

239
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:40,861
[Johnny sighs]

240
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:45,324
[thinking] <i>Wh... what is that?
Are those teeth?</i>

241
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:48,077
<i>My god, they're monstrous.</i>

242
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,037
<i>What else is under that bandage?</i>

243
00:13:51,288 --> 00:13:53,707
<i>That... that's not a hole in his cheek...</i>

244
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:56,502
<i>His mouth... it's split from ear to ear.</i>

245
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:58,712
What you been up to, Johnny?

246
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:01,841
Why did all these flies
decide to bunk with us?

247
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:03,717
Little bastards drive me nuts.

248
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:06,178
Shut the window, would you?

249
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,141
[grunts]

250
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:18,065
Johnny, shut the window, now!

251
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:21,026
This is worse than a couple flies!
How the hell did you miss it?

252
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:22,820
You're not gonna believe this.

253
00:14:24,238 --> 00:14:27,658
A huge bear carcass!
And something's been chewing on it.

254
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:29,743
Whatever did this
sure as shit wasn't human.

255
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:30,911
[Johnny gasps]

256
00:14:35,749 --> 00:14:36,917
Dio!

257
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:42,923
<i>♪ Steel Ball Run ♪</i>

258
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:46,051
Is... is this really happening?

259
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:48,345
He looks like a huge lizard.

260
00:14:48,846 --> 00:14:52,099
So Dio was a stand user all along?

261
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:53,809
[Gyro] Huh?

262
00:14:54,643 --> 00:14:56,478
- [tense music playing]
- [Gyro grunts]

263
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,856
Gyro!

264
00:14:58,939 --> 00:14:59,982
[Gyro grunts]

265
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,276
Uh...

266
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:03,360
[gasps]

267
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:05,237
[Dio growls]

268
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:06,780
- Aah!
- [roars]

269
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:08,032
Tusk, now!

270
00:15:08,115 --> 00:15:09,325
[mystical whirring]

271
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:11,368
[thinking] <i>It dodged them?!</i>

272
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:15,289
[Dio groaning]

273
00:15:15,372 --> 00:15:16,874
[roars]

274
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:21,587
I knew it! Dio wants us dead!
Just like all the other assailants!

275
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:23,297
- [Dio roars]
- [Johnny grunts]

276
00:15:24,131 --> 00:15:25,007
[gasps]

277
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:26,967
[grunts]

278
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:30,804
- [mystical whirring]
- [Johnny gasps]

279
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:34,975
Well, what do you know?
Our boy Dio's got some reflexes on him.

280
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:38,020
He just dodged my ball
like it was nothing.

281
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,856
One hell of a trick at this close a range.

282
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:42,650
[Dio growls]

283
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:44,902
[gasps]

284
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:49,031
[mystical whirring]

285
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:50,157
[roars]

286
00:15:51,158 --> 00:15:52,993
- What?
- Gyro!

287
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:55,287
- Above you!
- [roars]

288
00:15:55,871 --> 00:15:56,747
[grunts]

289
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:59,333
[roars]

290
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,585
What are you trying to pull off, Brando?

291
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:03,837
Find the next piece of the corpse
along the way?

292
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:06,632
Or kill us here
and take the one we've already got?

293
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:09,551
You'll pounce at the least little thing,
won't you?

294
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:12,262
Which means maybe, if things move slow,

295
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:15,766
you don't feel threatened by them
and hop out of the damn way.

296
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:17,476
[action music playing]

297
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:23,399
[chuckles]

298
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:26,902
[roars]

299
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:30,155
Turns out I put my steel ball in that can.

300
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:34,159
How I did it without opening the can,
though, that's the real trick.

301
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,036
[growls]

302
00:16:37,746 --> 00:16:38,998
[Gyro grunts]

303
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:39,999
Gyro!

304
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,962
[Gyro] He didn't like it.
But I don't think it really hurt him much.

305
00:16:45,546 --> 00:16:47,673
- Let's get out of here, Johnny!
- [tense music playing]

306
00:16:48,257 --> 00:16:50,759
[Gyro] Crawl like your life depends on it!
Hurry!

307
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:51,802
[growls]

308
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:52,845
[Johnny grunts]

309
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,889
[grunting]

310
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:57,641
What the hell happened to him, Gyro?

311
00:16:57,725 --> 00:16:59,101
We've seen some crazy stands,

312
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:01,895
but nothing
that turned people into lizard things!

313
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:04,023
That "lizard thing" is a dinosaur.

314
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:05,274
I don't know how he did it,

315
00:17:05,357 --> 00:17:07,901
but I definitely feel below him
in the food chain right now.

316
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:10,529
[Johnny] Dinosaur?!
I don't even know what that is.

317
00:17:10,612 --> 00:17:11,989
How could you not?

318
00:17:12,072 --> 00:17:14,533
They're a bunch of big reptiles
that went extinct.

319
00:17:14,616 --> 00:17:15,993
Some were bigger than elephants.

320
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:20,789
"Dinosaur." Latin for "terrible lizard."
A scholar named Owen coined the name.

321
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,333
But this one's smaller than an elephant.

322
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:24,960
Not the point, Johnny.

323
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:27,046
The point is
that they've been extinct forever.

324
00:17:27,129 --> 00:17:29,089
They were dead
before man walked the Earth.

325
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:32,760
[Johnny] Why does Dio have
the powers of a creature from so long ago?

326
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:35,179
Maybe it has something to do with fossils.

327
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:39,016
They've found dinosaur bones
in the high cliffs over Colorado.

328
00:17:39,099 --> 00:17:41,852
Turns out the Rockies
are full of the damn things.

329
00:17:41,935 --> 00:17:42,770
[gasps]

330
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:45,773
[mystical chimes play]

331
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:49,568
[mysterious music playing]

332
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:02,956
[gasps]

333
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,166
[breathing shakily]

334
00:18:06,752 --> 00:18:08,796
- [grunts]
- [tense music playing]

335
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:11,673
Oh, damn it all.
This door's about to give way.

336
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:13,342
Let's escape down the cliff, Johnny!

337
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:15,010
I won't. I can't risk it.

338
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:19,515
If Dio's going after the remains,
we have to defeat him, Gyro.

339
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:21,475
If you're smart,
you'll stay right where you are.

340
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:24,311
Dio can't track anything
that isn't moving.

341
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:25,354
What did you say?

342
00:18:27,314 --> 00:18:28,816
[Dio roars]

343
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:35,239
[Johnny] Don't move, Gyro. No matter what.

344
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:39,701
I don't know why,
but Dio only sees movement.

345
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:42,162
Maybe it's a dinosaur thing?

346
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:55,467
Stay still. You can't even blink.

347
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:58,762
I'm sure I'm right. Yeah, like before.

348
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:01,807
He couldn't see
the coffee right in front of him.

349
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:02,766
[Gyro grunts softly]

350
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:07,396
It worked.

351
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:10,149
He assumes we went down the cliffside.

352
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:15,737
[both gasp]

353
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:21,493
[whispers] Johnny,
do you think he figured it out?

354
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:22,911
He's coming back.

355
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:25,455
[grunts]

356
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:26,915
[Dio growls softly]

357
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,336
Keep it together, Gyro.

358
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,589
Dio has no clue we're here.

359
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:36,008
He smells the dead bear, that's all.

360
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:43,307
[Gyro grunts quietly]

361
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:46,351
[shudders]

362
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:54,359
Did we pull it off? Where did he go,
that scaly son of a bitch?

363
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:55,319
[Johnny sighs]

364
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:57,196
Did we throw him off our trail yet,
yes or no?

365
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:58,280
Quiet.

366
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:03,577
[Johnny gasps]

367
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:07,039
[thinking] <i>That's right.
Dio knows about it.</i>

368
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:11,585
<i>He saw the steel ball in action
back during the first stage of the race.</i>

369
00:20:12,711 --> 00:20:14,296
Gyro, this is bad!

370
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:16,340
Dio knows that your balls
will always return to you

371
00:20:16,423 --> 00:20:18,884
at the end of their journey,
no matter what.

372
00:20:19,384 --> 00:20:21,428
Nothing can stop it from coming back.

373
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:24,765
He's gonna follow it home,
and when it gets there, you're dead!

374
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,185
[Gyro grunts]

375
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:33,148
No! Gyro!

376
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:35,776
- [Gyro grunts]
- [mystical whirring]

377
00:20:39,613 --> 00:20:40,656
[growls]

378
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:46,453
You gotta calm down, Johnny.

379
00:20:46,536 --> 00:20:51,208
As you saw for yourself, the ball
flattened my legs and kept rolling along.

380
00:20:52,459 --> 00:20:54,044
And a damn good thing that it did

381
00:20:54,628 --> 00:20:57,631
'cause now he thinks we're somewhere
on the other side of that wall.

382
00:20:57,714 --> 00:20:59,216
[roars]

383
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:04,471
- Finally! He went straight down the cliff!
- [Gyro sighs]

384
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:08,976
Johnny, you know
those letters scrawled into your arm?

385
00:21:09,059 --> 00:21:13,188
{\an8}I just figured something out about them.
It has to do with how they're positioned.

386
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:15,232
[Johnny] Huh?

387
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:17,609
[grunts softly]

388
00:21:18,235 --> 00:21:19,069
[gasps]

389
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:21,029
[mysterious music playing]

390
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:22,030
What?

391
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:26,076
[gasps]

392
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:30,163
Gyro, there's... something odd about this.

393
00:21:31,748 --> 00:21:33,208
[faint growling]

394
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:37,170
Why does it sound like
there's something below us?

395
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:38,755
There is.

396
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,799
But what are we hearing, exactly?

397
00:21:40,882 --> 00:21:41,967
[gasps]

398
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:43,260
[creature groaning]

399
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:45,262
Gyro! It's moving!

400
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:50,684
[growls]

401
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:52,227
Oh, come on!

402
00:21:52,811 --> 00:21:56,315
This dinosaur is even bigger.
And it was a dead bear before.

403
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:59,776
Dio's stand ability,
it's the worst one yet!

404
00:22:01,778 --> 00:22:04,448
[roars]

405
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:08,035
[horse trotting]

406
00:22:08,118 --> 00:22:11,163
[energetic music playing]

407
00:22:11,246 --> 00:22:13,248
[lyrics in Japanese]

408
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:23,258
<i>♪ Steel Ball Run ♪</i>

409
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:26,553
<i>♪ Steel Ball Run ♪</i>

410
00:22:26,636 --> 00:22:29,473
<i>♪ Steel Ball Run ♪</i>

411
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:31,558
[lyrics in Japanese]

412
00:23:22,609 --> 00:23:25,862
{\an8}<i>♪ Steel Ball Run ♪</i>

413
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:28,865
{\an8}<i>♪ Steel Ball Run ♪</i>

414
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:32,035
{\an8}<i>♪ Steel Ball Run ♪</i>

415
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:35,080
{\an8}[lyrics in Japanese]

